{"id":170861,"accession_number":"2013.338","share_license_status":"CC0","tombstone":"A princess reclining on a terrace with attendants, c. 1730–1740. India, Mughal, 18th century. Gum tempera and gold on paper; page: 20.6 x 30.6 cm (8 1/8 x 12 1/16 in.). The Cleveland Museum of Art, Gift in honor of Madeline Neves Clapp; Gift of Mrs. Henry White Cannon by exchange; Bequest of Louise T. Cooper; Leonard C. Hanna Jr. Fund; From the Catherine and Ralph Benkaim Collection, 2013.338","current_location":null,"title":"A princess reclining on a terrace with attendants","creation_date":"c. 1730–1740","creation_date_earliest":1725,"creation_date_latest":1745,"artists_tags":[],"culture":["India, Mughal, 18th century"],"technique":"Gum tempera and gold on paper","support_materials":[],"department":"Indian and Southeast Asian Art","collection":"Indian Art - Mughal","type":"Painting","measurements":"Page: 20.6 x 30.6 cm (8 1/8 x 12 1/16 in.)","dimensions":{"painting only":{"height":0.157,"height_inch":6,"height_inch_fraction":0.1875,"width":0.26,"width_inch":10,"width_inch_fraction":0.25},"page":{"height":0.206,"height_inch":8,"height_inch_fraction":0.125,"width":0.306,"width_inch":12,"width_inch_fraction":0.0625}},"state_of_the_work":null,"edition_of_the_work":null,"copyright":null,"inscriptions":[],"exhibitions":{"current":[{"id":203111,"title":"Art and Stories from Mughal India","description":"<i>Art and Stories from Mughal India</i>. The Cleveland Museum of Art, Cleveland, OH (organizer) (July 31-October 23, 2016).","opening_date":"2016-07-31T04:00:00"}],"legacy":[{"description":"The Cleveland Museum of Art (7/31/2016-10/23/2016); Art and Stories from Mughal India, cat. 77, p. 297.","opening_date":"2016-07-31T00:00:00"}]},"provenance":[{"description":"Sotheby’s, London, Important Western and Oriental Manuscripts and Miniatures, 11 April 1961, lot 35","citations":[],"footnotes":[],"date":null,"sortorder":1},{"description":"Collection of Prince Michael Radziwill (b. 1907), London","citations":[],"footnotes":[],"date":null,"sortorder":2},{"description":"Christie’s, London, Art and Textiles of the Islamic and Indian World, 7 October 2011, lot 391","citations":[],"footnotes":[],"date":null,"sortorder":3},{"description":"Ramesh Kapoor, New York, until March 2012","citations":[],"footnotes":[],"date":null,"sortorder":4}],"find_spot":null,"related_works":[],"former_accession_numbers":[],"did_you_know":"White is the color worn by widows.","early_education_description":null,"artlens_description":null,"description":"This scene presents an idealized view of the life of a Mughal princess. Bejeweled and dressed in costly garments, she reclines on a couch set up on a white marble terrace. She watches two musicians sing and clap time, and a companion pours for her a cup of liquor. Two attendants stand behind, one waving a whisk to keep away the insects and another holding a box of paan, a betel-leaf preparation for freshening the breath. At the far right an older woman of the harem holds a fan while enjoying a hookah.","external_resources":{"wikidata":["https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q60482102"],"internet_archive":["https://archive.org/details/clevelandart-2013.338-a-princess-reclining"]},"citations":[],"url":"https://clevelandart.org/art/2013.338","images":{"annotation":null,"web":{"url":"https://openaccess-cdn.clevelandart.org/2013.338/2013.338_web.jpg","width":"900","height":"562","filesize":"189107","filename":"2013.338_web.jpg"},"print":{"url":"https://openaccess-cdn.clevelandart.org/2013.338/2013.338_print.jpg","width":"3400","height":"2124","filesize":"1947424","filename":"2013.338_print.jpg"},"full":{"url":"https://openaccess-cdn.clevelandart.org/2013.338/2013.338_full.tif","width":"7710","height":"4817","filesize":"111449580","filename":"2013.338_full.tif"}},"alternate_images":[{"web":{"url":"https://openaccess-cdn.clevelandart.org/2013.338/2013.338_alt0_web.jpg","width":"900","height":"616","filesize":"133964"},"print":{"url":"https://openaccess